{"repositoryId":1411463452,"availability":"available","full":"aristoteliss/anarchon","name":"anarchon","description":"Distributed cron and interval scheduling with no leader and no distributed locks. One atomic claim selects one instance per scheduled run.","category":"Business","language":"TypeScript","stars":2,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-09T07:35:21Z","updated":"2026-10-18T15:51:38Z","license":"AGPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://aristoteliss.github.io/anarchon/","topics":["background-jobs","cron","distributed-scheduler","distributed-systems","interval","job-scheduling","leaderless","nats","nodejs","postgresql","rabbitmq","redis","scheduler","sqlite","typescript","valkey"],"demo":"https://aristoteliss.github.io/anarchon/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T16:51:53.741Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-18T16:51:53.741Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-18T16:51:53.741Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T16:51:53.741Z","discoveredVia":[],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-18T16:51:53.741Z","stars":2,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Node.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Documentation · Quick start · Guarantees and limits · Examples · License","Leaderless scheduling for Node.js clusters. Run the same jobs in every instance; an atomic claim in Redis, Valkey, PostgreSQL or SQLite selects one runner for each scheduled slot. The default lease strategy retries after a runner stops renewing its lease. That gives at-least-once execution after failures, not exactly-once side effects: handlers should be idempotent, and a frozen runner can briefly overlap its replacement.","anarchon also handles what goes wrong in real clusters:"],"features":["jobs that run longer than their interval","an instance crashing or freezing mid-run","rolling deploys, and every instance restarting at once"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/aristoteliss/anarchon/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"91635613150fa4d1c8ca83a1fcafbbd3e26e79eef9af30f222e2aef30d50ab09","ex